Installed `balloons`, `textBalloons` and the `useBalloons` hook (`@/components/ui/balloons`, with three helper files beside it).

```tsx
import { balloons, textBalloons, useBalloons } from "@/components/ui/balloons";

// Anywhere in the browser: over the whole page.
balloons();
textBalloons([{ text: "HAPPY", color: "#FA4616EE", fontSize: 120 }]);

// In a component: contained in an element, stopped on unmount.
const stage = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
const { release, releaseText, stop } = useBalloons({ containerRef: stage });
```

Both functions return a promise that resolves when the effect ends, and take `{ container, signal, reducedMotion }`. Under reduced motion nothing flies: one still frame fades in and out (`reducedMotion: "skip"` does nothing instead). The layers are `aria-hidden`; announce the event itself in your UI.

Text balloons draw each letter as an SVG image, which cannot see your page's fonts. The family comes from `--balloons-font-family` (default `ui-rounded, system-ui, sans-serif`). Upstream uses the Sniglet typeface (SIL Open Font License), which is not bundled here: to use it, download it (Google Fonts or `@fontsource/sniglet`), serve the file, then `const fontFace = await balloonFontFace("Sniglet", "/fonts/sniglet-800.woff2")`, set `--balloons-font-family: Sniglet, system-ui` and pass `{ fontFace }`; keep the font's license with it.

Ported from arturbien/balloons-js (MIT, copyright 2024 Artur Bień); the license notice is at the end of every file.
